      "On a stormy night in his London chambers at the Temple, Pip was visited by a rugged, weathered traveler in a heavy seaman's coat. To Pip's utter horror, the man revealed himself as Abel Magwitch, the terrifying convict he had helped in the churchyard marshes long ago! Magwitch had made a vast fortune in New South Wales as a sheep farmer, and had devoted every penny to making Pip a wealthy, fine gentleman.",
      "In that shattering moment, Pip's proud delusions crumbled: Miss Havisham was not his benefactor, and Estella was never intended for him! Though initially repulsed by the coarse old convict, Pip's noble heart asserted itself. Magwitch was a hunted felon who had risked the gallows to return to England merely to gaze upon the gentleman he had created.",
