      "Aboard the Pequod, Captain Ahab gathered his crew around the mast, nailing an ounce of Spanish gold to the wood: 'Whosoever of ye raises me that white-headed whale with a wrinkled brow and a crooked jaw, he shall have this gold ounce, boys!' The harpooners—Queequeg, Tashtego, and Daggoo—drank grog from the hollow sockets of their harpoon irons, shouting oaths to hunt the White Whale to the death.",
      "The fateful encounter took place in the Pacific equator. For three days, Ahab chased Moby Dick in his whaleboat. The White Whale breached from the azure deep like an avalanche of snow, tossing boats into matchwood and snapping harpoon lines with contemptuous ease. On the third day, Moby Dick turned upon the Pequod itself, ramming the ship's bow with titanic fury!",
      "As the doomed ship sank beneath the waves, Ahab cast his final harpoon: 'Towards thee I roll, thou all-destroying but unconquering whale; to the last I grapple with thee; from hell's heart I stab at thee; for hate's sake I spit my last breath at thee!' The flying harpoon line caught Ahab round the neck, dragging him into the watery depths. The vortex sucked down the entire crew, leaving Ishmael alone, floating upon Queequeg's wooden coffin, rescued on the following day by the Rachel, orphaned and delivered to tell the immortal tale.",
